# instance-log ring never prunes numbered strays beyond keep+16 after a C2C_INSTANCE_LOG_KEEP reduction

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

C2c_instance_log.rotate (c2c_instance_log.ml:69-76) removes only log.<n> through log.<n+16>; a host that previously ran a larger C2C_INSTANCE_LOG_KEEP (say 50) and is later reduced to 3 keeps log.20 through log.50 forever - the shift never touches them and the live-path cap never fires on them. Bounded disk leak.

## Fix direction

Sweep all log.<digits> with index >= keep at rotation (readdir-based, not a fixed +16 window).

